{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"scalar multiplication of a matrix scalar multiplication of a matrix","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix.md","fileName":"Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 19:44\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Matrix and Vector Computation]] · [[FEM Mathematical Foundations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matrix and Vector Computation","FEM Mathematical Foundations","Matrix","Matrix Addition","Zero Matrix","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","finiteelementanalysis_aprimer.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"scalar multiplication of a matrix scalar multiplication of a matrix","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix.md","fileName":"Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix","heading":"Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Scalar multiplication multiplies every entry of a [[Matrix]] by the same number. For $A=(a_{ij})$ and scalar $k$, the matrix $kA$ has entries $ka_{ij}$ and keeps the dimensions of $A$.\n\nIt distributes over [[Matrix Addition]] and over addition of scalars. Multiplication by zero produces the [[Zero Matrix]], while multiplication by $-1$ produces the additive inverse of the matrix.\n\nFinite element characteristic matrices often appear as a geometric matrix multiplied by a scalar material-and-size factor, such as axial rigidity divided by element length. Scalar multiplication preserves the matrix pattern while changing its physical scale.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matrix and Vector Computation","FEM Mathematical Foundations","Matrix","Matrix Addition","Zero Matrix","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","finiteelementanalysis_aprimer.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"scalar multiplication of a matrix scalar multiplication of a matrix","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix.md","fileName":"Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Scalar Multiplication of a Matrix","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf]]\n\n[[finiteelementanalysis_aprimer.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Matrix and Vector Computation","FEM Mathematical Foundations","Matrix","Matrix Addition","Zero Matrix","appliedlinearalgebraandoptimizationusingmatlab.pdf","finiteelementanalysis_aprimer.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}